1
00:00:00,820 --> 00:00:06,300
体中の細胞に火を起こすように

2
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:11,000
めいっぱいに空気を吸い込んだ

3
00:00:11,640 --> 00:00:14,520
血と汗を煮えに

4
00:00:14,520 --> 00:00:17,220
憧れを精化に

5
00:00:17,220 --> 00:00:21,260
フルーボリュームで叫べよ

6
00:00:21,260 --> 00:00:23,060
光あれ

7
00:00:23,060 --> 00:00:53,040
Oh, yeah.

8
00:00:53,060 --> 00:00:59,500
光あれ、大地へ避ける理由はたったひとつ

9
00:00:59,500 --> 00:01:04,000
光あれ、もっと眩く俺は僕

10
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:10,220
光あれ、君の今日の輝きが

11
00:01:10,220 --> 00:01:17,460
迷える友の明日を照らすよ

12
00:01:17,460 --> 00:01:25,900
光あれ、君の日を照らすよ

13
00:01:25,900 --> 00:01:27,460
光あれ、君の日を照らすよ

14
00:01:27,460 --> 00:01:29,460
光あれ、君の日を照らすよ

15
00:01:29,460 --> 00:01:59,440
光あれ、君の日を照らすよ

16
00:01:59,460 --> 00:02:29,440
光あれ、君の日を照らすよ

17
00:02:29,440 --> 00:02:35,440
Listen up children. Reblocking works. It takes persistence, training, and endurance.

18
00:02:36,440 --> 00:02:40,440
And when you master it, you'll always get the last laugh.

19
00:02:41,440 --> 00:02:43,440
One chance!

20
00:02:44,440 --> 00:02:47,440
Get that chance ball!

21
00:02:50,440 --> 00:02:55,440
That leaves us with no choice but to attack.

22
00:02:57,440 --> 00:02:58,440
A minus tempo.

23
00:03:00,440 --> 00:03:01,440
Back attack!

24
00:03:02,440 --> 00:03:03,440
Do it!

25
00:03:03,440 --> 00:03:05,440
Get it Taichi!

26
00:03:12,440 --> 00:03:13,440
Shirabu!

27
00:03:14,440 --> 00:03:15,440
What?

28
00:03:15,440 --> 00:03:17,440
It's a strike!

29
00:03:17,440 --> 00:03:18,440
And now!

30
00:03:22,440 --> 00:03:23,440
Hinaja!

31
00:03:26,440 --> 00:03:28,440
Follow up Kageyama!

32
00:03:28,440 --> 00:03:29,440
Hey!

33
00:03:29,440 --> 00:03:30,440
You okay dude?

34
00:03:30,440 --> 00:03:31,440
Yeah!

35
00:03:31,440 --> 00:03:32,440
It's in!

36
00:03:32,440 --> 00:03:33,440
Got it!

37
00:03:33,440 --> 00:03:34,440
Damn!

38
00:03:34,440 --> 00:03:36,440
They returned it to a bad spot!

39
00:03:40,440 --> 00:03:41,440
Well, no time to hesitate!

40
00:03:41,440 --> 00:03:42,440
Pushylock out!

41
00:03:42,440 --> 00:03:43,440
It's off!

42
00:03:43,440 --> 00:03:44,440
Damn!

43
00:03:44,440 --> 00:03:46,440
I wish that set was for me!

44
00:03:46,440 --> 00:03:47,440
But...

45
00:03:47,440 --> 00:03:51,440
I guess I do want to see his spikes!

46
00:03:51,440 --> 00:03:52,440
It's just that...

47
00:03:52,440 --> 00:03:56,440
Sometimes that's frustrating too!

48
00:03:57,440 --> 00:03:58,440
Here it comes!

49
00:03:58,440 --> 00:04:07,440
This is the first time today that they're using a three-man block to stop a straight!

50
00:04:07,440 --> 00:04:15,440
So when it's the final push, we will use a three-man block to close out a straight, not a cross-court shot.

51
00:04:16,440 --> 00:04:19,440
We'll use a few plays to prepare the bait for this trap.

52
00:04:21,440 --> 00:04:28,440
With the repetition of our three-man blocks, we'll make it look like we have a flaw, that we just use them to cover cross-court shots.

53
00:04:28,440 --> 00:04:33,440
As long as our timing is spot-on, there won't be any opportunity for the ball to go anywhere else.

54
00:04:34,440 --> 00:04:38,440
We'll let Ishiwaka get comfortable in knowing we have a hole in our defense.

55
00:04:39,440 --> 00:04:41,440
He'll think he can send us straight right through.

56
00:04:41,440 --> 00:04:54,440
Even though he was breaking his form, he was still able to nail a cross-court shot!

57
00:05:02,440 --> 00:05:03,440
Damn it!

58
00:05:03,440 --> 00:05:05,440
Damn it all!

59
00:05:05,440 --> 00:05:07,440
It's just too damn good!

60
00:05:11,440 --> 00:05:12,440
Damn it!

61
00:05:16,440 --> 00:05:17,440
Asai!

62
00:05:18,440 --> 00:05:19,440
Save it!

63
00:05:33,440 --> 00:05:34,440
Chance ball!

64
00:05:36,440 --> 00:05:38,440
Damn it!

65
00:05:38,440 --> 00:05:42,020
Ten's coming!

66
00:05:45,100 --> 00:05:47,500
He's not flying up front yet.

67
00:05:48,540 --> 00:05:52,480
He's slowing down his tempo from Minus down to first.

68
00:05:53,760 --> 00:05:56,460
Then, he's joining the group.

69
00:05:58,900 --> 00:06:00,240
Shit, no way!

70
00:06:08,440 --> 00:06:10,640
Yeah, right there.

71
00:06:35,660 --> 00:06:37,100
Ah!

72
00:06:38,440 --> 00:06:49,740
Volleyball is a sport where height advantage can take you far.

73
00:06:50,280 --> 00:06:52,980
Naturally, the taller the player, the stronger they are.

74
00:06:53,740 --> 00:06:57,520
However, it is also a strength to perfect your individual skill.

75
00:06:58,320 --> 00:07:02,140
New defenses, attacks, and setups are born in the fray,

76
00:07:02,580 --> 00:07:05,220
which makes this great sport ever-revolving.

77
00:07:05,220 --> 00:07:09,640
Strength can come in many forms.

78
00:07:11,120 --> 00:07:14,260
As the great coach Ari Selinger once said,

79
00:07:15,480 --> 00:07:20,600
there is no reason to not believe that advancement and revolution will come in the future.

80
00:07:21,460 --> 00:07:23,880
And it has never been more true.

81
00:07:35,220 --> 00:07:46,780
Oh, my...

82
00:07:46,780 --> 00:07:49,880
What?

83
00:07:49,880 --> 00:07:57,300
What? This can't be for real?

84
00:07:59,800 --> 00:08:03,900
Hey, that's my little brother out there. The tall one with the glasses.

85
00:08:04,660 --> 00:08:08,820
We did it. We really did it. I can't believe it.

86
00:08:19,880 --> 00:08:21,880
No!

87
00:08:21,880 --> 00:08:23,880
No!

88
00:08:23,880 --> 00:08:25,880
No!

89
00:08:25,880 --> 00:08:27,880
No!

90
00:08:27,880 --> 00:08:29,880
No!

91
00:08:33,880 --> 00:08:37,880
Farewell, my paradise.

92
00:08:37,880 --> 00:08:39,880
Hey, time to line up.

93
00:08:39,880 --> 00:08:41,880
I can't, I can't walk.

94
00:08:41,880 --> 00:08:43,880
Come on, Hilda.

95
00:08:43,880 --> 00:08:47,880
Hey! What are you doing, please? Just look off me!

96
00:08:49,880 --> 00:08:51,880
Thank you for the game!

97
00:08:59,880 --> 00:09:01,880
What a game...

98
00:09:09,880 --> 00:09:11,880
At least try to look sad.

99
00:09:11,880 --> 00:09:15,880
Ushiwaka, you know, you're an enormous, emotionless bastard.

100
00:09:15,880 --> 00:09:17,880
Thank you very much!

101
00:09:19,880 --> 00:09:29,880
Would you say Karasano's number ten is about the same height as me?

102
00:09:29,880 --> 00:09:31,880
Uh, uh, yeah, about.

103
00:09:31,880 --> 00:09:35,880
Well, I suppose he'll keep growing, huh?

104
00:09:35,880 --> 00:09:41,880
Although, the more ambitious his goals, the more he's going to struggle.

105
00:09:41,880 --> 00:09:46,880
Sorry, Hinata. We tried to close out that straight, but didn't make it in time. Is your face okay?

106
00:09:46,880 --> 00:09:47,880
Oh! I'm fine!

107
00:09:47,880 --> 00:09:51,880
Don't give the scrub too much credit. The ball did come right to him, after all.

108
00:09:51,880 --> 00:09:55,880
That Kageyama? He really played a tight game.

109
00:09:55,880 --> 00:09:57,880
I didn't want to acknowledge that.

110
00:09:57,880 --> 00:10:03,880
Although I think, that when Four Eyes came back, he laid out a game plan for everyone.

111
00:10:03,880 --> 00:10:06,880
Yeah, something about closing out Ushiwaka's straights.

112
00:10:06,880 --> 00:10:10,880
I'd assume that's why after his serve, Kageyama switched places with short stuff.

113
00:10:10,880 --> 00:10:12,880
He was in the cross path.

114
00:10:12,880 --> 00:10:16,880
And Nishinoya wasn't there to save the day.

115
00:10:16,880 --> 00:10:22,880
So that's why he was prepared to set it so quickly, huh? Your pupil has learned your teachings well.

116
00:10:22,880 --> 00:10:25,880
He's not my pupil!

117
00:10:25,880 --> 00:10:32,880
And then on top of that, he somehow managed to adjust his tempo to synchronize with that erratic little shrimp.

118
00:10:32,880 --> 00:10:35,880
He just pisses me off so much.

119
00:10:35,880 --> 00:10:41,880
Well, if it makes you feel any better, I think they were only able to pull off this win thanks to that first year with the glasses.

120
00:10:41,880 --> 00:10:47,880
I guess that little runt is definitely the kind of spiker you want to keep sending your sets.

121
00:10:47,880 --> 00:10:50,880
Probably helps keep Kageyama on his toes.

122
00:10:50,880 --> 00:10:53,880
Alright, well I say we get out of here.

123
00:10:53,880 --> 00:10:56,880
I don't want to choke on my own barf at this awards ceremony.

124
00:10:56,880 --> 00:10:59,880
You're still a piece of crap, you know that?

125
00:10:59,880 --> 00:11:00,880
Yeah!

126
00:11:02,880 --> 00:11:05,880
Thank you for coming to support us!

127
00:11:06,880 --> 00:11:08,880
Thank you for coming!

128
00:11:08,880 --> 00:11:10,880
Good job guys!

129
00:11:10,880 --> 00:11:11,880
You guys are amazing!

130
00:11:11,880 --> 00:11:13,880
You're going to be proof and proof!

131
00:11:21,880 --> 00:11:22,880
Let's go!

132
00:11:23,880 --> 00:11:24,880
He touched you!

133
00:11:24,880 --> 00:11:25,880
Sugawara!

134
00:11:25,880 --> 00:11:26,880
I'll see you again!

135
00:11:26,880 --> 00:11:28,880
Congrats on the win!

136
00:11:38,880 --> 00:11:41,880
Thank you everyone!

137
00:11:45,880 --> 00:11:46,880
Hey man!

138
00:11:46,880 --> 00:11:47,880
You okay?

139
00:11:47,880 --> 00:11:48,880
Uh...

140
00:11:48,880 --> 00:11:49,880
Uh...

141
00:11:49,880 --> 00:11:50,880
Yeah...

142
00:11:50,880 --> 00:11:52,880
I can't wrap my head around it.

143
00:11:54,880 --> 00:11:55,880
I never realized...

144
00:11:55,880 --> 00:11:57,880
That we could lose.

145
00:11:59,880 --> 00:12:00,880
Yeah...

146
00:12:01,880 --> 00:12:02,880
I...

147
00:12:02,880 --> 00:12:04,880
Don't think anyone else here did either.

148
00:12:04,880 --> 00:12:05,880
Uh...

149
00:12:05,880 --> 00:12:06,880
No...

150
00:12:06,880 --> 00:12:07,880
Uh...

151
00:12:07,880 --> 00:12:08,880
I...

152
00:12:08,880 --> 00:12:09,880
Uh...

153
00:12:09,880 --> 00:12:10,880
Uh...

154
00:12:10,880 --> 00:12:11,880
Uh...

155
00:12:11,880 --> 00:12:12,880
Uh...

156
00:12:12,880 --> 00:12:13,880
Uh...

157
00:12:13,880 --> 00:12:14,880
Uh...

158
00:12:14,880 --> 00:12:15,880
Uh...

159
00:12:15,880 --> 00:12:18,880
After the ceremony, load the bus...

160
00:12:18,880 --> 00:12:31,960
After the ceremony, load the bus.

161
00:12:32,680 --> 00:12:34,760
We'll have our team huddle after we get back home.

162
00:12:35,780 --> 00:12:36,160
Right.

163
00:12:36,360 --> 00:12:36,600
Right.

164
00:12:39,560 --> 00:12:42,080
Then, 100 serves for each of you.

165
00:12:48,880 --> 00:12:56,140
Everyone, really great job.

166
00:12:56,800 --> 00:13:00,540
I'm so, I'm so proud of you guys.

167
00:13:01,160 --> 00:13:03,620
Dai Chi, amazing job.

168
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:04,680
Well done.

169
00:13:04,960 --> 00:13:06,520
That three-man block was sweet.

170
00:13:07,080 --> 00:13:10,840
Even if your thighs feel like they're splitting, handle the mid-air fights for me.

171
00:13:11,720 --> 00:13:13,360
Just keeping my promise.

172
00:13:16,360 --> 00:13:17,360
Tsukishima!

173
00:13:18,880 --> 00:13:23,460
No matter what anyone else says, you, son, are the MVP today.

174
00:13:23,780 --> 00:13:26,420
Well, it does get exhausting always being the MVP.

175
00:13:26,680 --> 00:13:29,000
I'll let you carry the title today, Tsukishima.

176
00:13:29,460 --> 00:13:32,240
You're more like the MVP in being loud and obnoxious.

177
00:13:39,960 --> 00:13:43,200
Lushiwaka, I saw you got pissed off at the very end.

178
00:13:45,220 --> 00:13:48,440
Normally, you would have either regrouped or let someone else go after it.

179
00:13:48,880 --> 00:13:53,500
Gave me the chills watching your reaction.

180
00:13:56,680 --> 00:14:00,100
I wanted to tell him personally that I'm stronger than he is.

181
00:14:02,100 --> 00:14:02,620
Oh.

182
00:14:02,620 --> 00:14:04,880
I wanted to rub it in.

183
00:14:05,920 --> 00:14:07,340
Pretty immature of me.

184
00:14:09,580 --> 00:14:13,040
Aren't most people's motivations pretty childish anyways?

185
00:14:13,040 --> 00:14:16,200
That was a bad-ass trade.

186
00:14:16,780 --> 00:14:19,100
I felt like I met a new Ushiwaka today.

187
00:14:22,940 --> 00:14:25,320
I'm going to quit volleyball after high school.

188
00:14:25,320 --> 00:14:32,600
But when I see you playing professionally on television, I'm going to brag to everyone that we were BFFs back in the day.

189
00:14:32,900 --> 00:14:34,140
So make me proud, okay?

190
00:14:35,100 --> 00:14:35,540
Sure.

191
00:14:36,820 --> 00:14:42,540
And when they make a documentary about you, they can totally interview me as one of your old volleyball buddies.

192
00:14:42,540 --> 00:14:54,240
Ushiwaka was so damn amazing.

193
00:14:54,240 --> 00:15:01,540
Shouyo Hinata and Tobio Kageyama from the concrete.

194
00:15:04,340 --> 00:15:05,860
We'll beat you next time.

195
00:15:07,580 --> 00:15:09,860
Next time we go head-to-head, we'll still win!

196
00:15:09,940 --> 00:15:12,740
And I'm going to make you admit that I'm even better than Oikawa!

197
00:15:12,740 --> 00:15:33,100
Suki!

198
00:15:33,720 --> 00:15:35,400
The ceremony's about to begin!

199
00:15:36,280 --> 00:15:37,580
Is something wrong?

200
00:15:37,960 --> 00:15:42,540
I said I was hoping to stop a few of his spikes, but I was only able to stop one.

201
00:15:42,740 --> 00:15:44,920
I had five sets to do it, too.

202
00:15:46,320 --> 00:15:48,900
I'm so...worthless.

203
00:15:48,940 --> 00:15:50,240
Suki! You're not worthless!

204
00:15:50,620 --> 00:15:51,520
What's wrong with you?

205
00:15:52,040 --> 00:15:52,180
What?

206
00:15:53,080 --> 00:15:54,640
Stop beating yourself up!

207
00:15:54,940 --> 00:15:56,320
We're going to nationals!

208
00:15:56,660 --> 00:15:58,260
But first, the ceremony!

209
00:16:10,260 --> 00:16:10,580
Hm.

210
00:16:12,740 --> 00:16:20,480
You're winners of the Miyagi Prefectural Playoffs, I present to you, Karasuno High School.

211
00:16:21,180 --> 00:16:25,080
With their victory, this concludes the qualifying tournament for our area.

212
00:16:25,860 --> 00:16:30,860
You will be the representatives for our prefecture at the High School Boys Spring National Tournament.

213
00:16:30,860 --> 00:16:34,440
I present this award to commend you a great performance.

214
00:16:36,660 --> 00:16:37,260
Congratulations.

215
00:16:42,560 --> 00:16:48,440
Ladies and gentlemen, please give praise to both schools for their outstanding performance.

216
00:16:48,440 --> 00:16:57,880
Let us also wish Karasuno High School the best of luck in January, when they will be attending the Spring National Playoffs in Tokyo.

217
00:16:57,880 --> 00:17:02,480
So please join me in giving everyone a big, warm round of applause.

218
00:17:02,480 --> 00:17:07,860
We're going!

219
00:17:07,860 --> 00:17:10,060
We're going!

220
00:17:10,060 --> 00:17:12,060
We're going!

221
00:17:12,060 --> 00:17:12,080
We're going!

222
00:17:12,860 --> 00:17:14,600
To Spring Nationals!

223
00:17:14,600 --> 00:17:15,400
We're going!

224
00:17:16,600 --> 00:17:18,180
We're going!

225
00:17:26,880 --> 00:17:27,120
Okay.

226
00:17:28,900 --> 00:17:30,340
Okay, boys.

227
00:17:30,340 --> 00:17:34,020
My uncles one-year-old toddler has better manners than these jokers.

228
00:17:34,160 --> 00:17:35,120
Really scolding me.

229
00:17:35,120 --> 00:17:38,120
Come on, you guys! You eating or you sleeping?

230
00:17:38,520 --> 00:17:42,280
Oh, Coach! I'm so... I'm so happy!

231
00:17:42,640 --> 00:17:45,260
Specs, that's awful sweet, but maybe you should slow down.

232
00:17:45,500 --> 00:17:47,780
And that's probably the eighth time you've said that.

233
00:17:49,280 --> 00:17:51,680
Hey, be careful not to break any dishes, okay?

234
00:17:52,260 --> 00:17:55,160
From here on out, it's time to really buckle down.

235
00:17:55,700 --> 00:17:57,660
We are going to get serious, Specs.

236
00:18:05,120 --> 00:18:18,720
Hey, is it true that the volleyball club is headed to Nationals?

237
00:18:18,940 --> 00:18:21,000
Wow, did you really not get to see the game?

238
00:18:21,160 --> 00:18:22,600
You missed out. It was amazing.

239
00:18:22,880 --> 00:18:23,320
Yeah?

240
00:18:24,080 --> 00:18:26,920
Our volleyball team's, like, legendary once again.

241
00:18:27,600 --> 00:18:28,080
Legendary?

242
00:18:28,240 --> 00:18:31,000
I heard there's a really scary third-year student in the club.

243
00:18:31,060 --> 00:18:33,500
I heard they also hang with a delinquent second-year, too.

244
00:18:33,500 --> 00:18:35,000
I hope you're not a hostage, Hinata.

245
00:18:35,160 --> 00:18:37,780
Their manager is, like, totally gorgeous, you guys.

246
00:18:37,880 --> 00:18:38,580
No way.

247
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:41,120
So, where's the national tournament being held?

248
00:18:42,940 --> 00:18:44,640
Tokyo's Metro Gym!

249
00:18:44,780 --> 00:18:45,180
Whoa!

250
00:18:46,360 --> 00:18:47,520
That's so cool!

251
00:18:47,920 --> 00:18:48,720
I know, right?

252
00:18:49,420 --> 00:18:52,580
Good grief. That idiot's already gotten a big head.

253
00:18:52,600 --> 00:18:54,020
So that means you're going too, Hinata?

254
00:18:54,300 --> 00:18:54,960
Of course!

255
00:18:55,660 --> 00:18:57,340
Shouyo's in charge of everyone's stuff.

256
00:18:57,560 --> 00:18:59,420
Like, gets lunches, carries the luggage.

257
00:18:59,840 --> 00:19:01,420
So he's the scary dude's water boy?

258
00:19:01,420 --> 00:19:04,580
Wrong! I play, thank you very much!

259
00:19:04,760 --> 00:19:05,840
Oh, that's real cute.

260
00:19:05,900 --> 00:19:07,600
Why is that so hard to believe?

261
00:19:09,960 --> 00:19:11,900
Hey, what are you drawing there?

262
00:19:12,440 --> 00:19:12,720
Hmm?

263
00:19:13,860 --> 00:19:15,680
Starting on the volleyball club poster.

